# For engine/worker/Dockerfile (build context = repo root). The worker needs
# engine/, templates/, config/test_companies/, and - since
# engine/notify/send_pack_ready_email.py shells out to `node` to render
# packReadyEmail() via app/scripts/render-pack-ready-email.ts, the one
# canonical TS email template - app/lib and app/scripts too (System-Status.md
# Finding 152: a blanket `app` exclusion here meant that script, and its
# cwd, never existed in the built image, so the pack-ready email has never
# actually sent in production). Everything else under app/ (the Next.js app
# itself, its node_modules/.next, and any real .env* file) stays out -
# Docker can't re-include a file under an excluded parent, so these are
# listed individually rather than as a single `app` line with exceptions.
.git
app/node_modules
app/.next
app/.env*
!app/.env*.example
out
packs
state
assets
templates/incoming
config/klipcorp_profile.json
config/contact.json
config/team_roster.json
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
